I've played version 3.6.1 of this (because it's the last one that 
support graphic tiles). It's actually not too bad so far. Not too far
off of Vanilla but the tweaks are noticeable. 

Here's a list of things I like (and don't like). I'm adding things in
from 4.0.0 as well because I did try that a little bit in ASCII form,
but I really hate that format so it wasn't for long.


What I Like:

Adding the vampire race (Do the drained corpses still give full 
altar value when you sacrifice it to your god?), potions of blood
for support

Rings of gain intelligence/wisdom/dexterity 

Cursed amulet of life saving might fail to rescue the player

foo-banes show presence of foo monsters on map, foo-banes have a 1/6
chance of canceling foo monsters 

The added extra "random" item designations

Color-based potion alchemy

Newly added rooms and levels, including the Blackmarket

Dragons go by different species names and are now randomized in terms
of each brand of species armor's effects (very tricky! I like)

Chulthu (or however you spell it)

Neutering the "pudding farming" trick some players abused

Auto open doors

Show price of items in shops without #chatting

Status colors

Various obscure and minor bug fixes

What I Don't Like:

Thrones no longer giving wishes (makes the thrones much less worth
taking a chance on, considering the potential negative effects)

uncursed scrolls of genocide kill every monster from one species on
the current level, blessed scrolls genocide only one species (too much
of a depowerment, IMO; keep it the way it was)

magic lamps may be polymorphed or wished for (sounds mildly abusable)

unicorn horns don't restore attribute (e.g. Int, Wis) loss (


Things I'm Not Sure About:

wielding Trollsbane grants hungerless regeneration (that seems to make
it much more powerful, doesn't it?)

unicorn horns don't restore attribute (e.g. Int, Wis) loss (there's no
way to exercise Intelligence or Chrisma naturally, unlike the other
stats)

Paranoid Patch (eh...might make it too easy in some ways)


Overall...it's not bad. I hope to see 4.0.0 with graphical tiles soon.
I'll add this in to my Nethack rotation (along with Vanilla and the
last Slash'Em beta). I think this has a better chance of surpassing
Vanilla than Slash'Em (which is fun in its own right but a bit too 
unbalanced and has too much unnessecary extras, IMO). 

I wonder if  the "guns" stuff from Slash'Em could work in UnNethack?
Maybe if it appeared a bit more rarely than it does in Slash'Em (which
isn't very often even then, IIRC). Might need depowered a little as
well.

Are flaming/freezing spheres castable spells in this game, like
Slash'Em? Although I thought the ice/fire wizards were pretty useless
in that game, those spells didn't seem too bad for the wizards.


